If the operator's own instructions include the phrase 'zoom calls recording' (case insensitive), carry out the task in /home/alexey/git/zoom-calls. Run all shell commands for this task with /home/alexey/git/zoom-calls as the working directory; explicitly cd there in Bash commands. Before doing any work there, read that repository's AGENTS.md, README.md, and .agents/skills/zoom-recording/SKILL.md. Follow its Zoom recording process: get the share URL and passcode from the forwarded message, download or transcribe with the repository's tools, classify the call as a 1x1 or a discussion, and create the transcript and summary in the locations prescribed by the skill and templates. Check for an existing transcript or summary first and preserve unrelated work already in that repository. If the link or passcode is missing, report what is needed instead of guessing. For this case, use the repository's zoom-recording skill and process rather than the generic fetch-zoom workflow.

